  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line.\n\n**Root cause:** `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` checked each line's item **name** against the SKU you passed in (`l.item.name != sku`). Widget's name is `'Widget'`, not `'sku-1'`, so it never matched and nothing was removed. I changed the check to `l.item.sku != sku`, which is the same field `Cart.add` uses to find a line.\n\n**Results:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 pass.\n- None of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, so they wouldn't have caught this bug. I didn't add a test for it.",
